Module EOS.SDK

The EOS.SDK module provides the standalone Epic Online Services foundation for
BlitzMax NG. Initialize once, create one or more platform instances, tick them
regularly on the main thread, release them, and then shut down the SDK.

The Epic SDK is a separate download and is not redistributed with this module.
Developer-portal product configuration and credentials must be supplied at
runtime and must not be committed to source control.

Platform.Auth() exposes Epic Account Services login and token operations.
Platform.Connect() exposes game-services identity login and Product User
creation. Both use retained request objects and listeners; call Platform.Tick()
until a terminal result is delivered. Releasing the platform cancels any
remaining requests before the native handle is released.

Platform.Stats() exposes stat ingestion and queries. A successful query fills
the SDK's local cache; use StatsCount(), CopyStatByIndex(), or CopyStatByName()
to copy managed values from it. Leave the query's StatNames array empty to
request all stats, and use EOS_STATS_TIME_UNDEFINED for an open time range.

Platform.Achievements() queries localized definitions and player progress into
the SDK cache. Its copy methods return independent BlitzMax objects, including
stat thresholds and current player stat information.
Explicit unlock operations are asynchronous. Unlock notification subscriptions
must be removed when no longer needed; platform release removes any remaining
subscriptions automatically.

See examples/auth_connect.bmx for a Developer Authentication Tool flow that
continues from Auth to Connect using the recommended Epic ID token.
See examples/stats.bmx for an Auth-to-Connect flow that ingests and queries a
stat configured in the Developer Portal.
See examples/achievements.bmx for definition and player-progress queries.

On macOS, build interactive Auth clients as GUI application bundles. The
tools/eos_auth_consent.bmx Max2D utility demonstrates Account Portal consent,
Developer Authentication Tool login, Connect, and Product User creation without
requiring MaxGUI.
